	(text "Switch inputs. One network: [4.7k pull-up to VPWR, ground-switched only] - SMF24A - 33k - node (15k, 10n, BAT54J to 3.3 V) - MCU." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 20.00 16.00 0) (effects (font (size 1.7 1.7)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "1f2dfb66-59ad-4ca3-b4f0-1ac5b46f5e63"))
	(text "Pull-ups go to VPWR, not 5 V / 3.3 V: those stay up parked, and a TR bit closed in Park would draw mA all night." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 20.00 20.00 0) (effects (font (size 1.7 1.7)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "c6ff7489-aa92-45fd-8f5c-1329cf8f3619"))
	(text "Levels: 14 V -> clamped; 9 V cranking -> 2.8 V (high-side) / 2.6 V (ground-switched) vs VIH 2.3 V. Open high-side reads 0." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 20.00 24.00 0) (effects (font (size 1.7 1.7)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "bfb70cb8-913b-479f-83d1-846883b8d91e"))
	(text "TR3A (64): on this 4R70W it is 12 V cranking in P/N, so the high-side network. A 4R100 (270R coded) needs a 2.2k" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 20.00 28.00 0) (effects (font (size 1.7 1.7)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "27dd8f55-9e87-407c-bc94-54bf5abee17b"))
	(text "pull-up to 3.3 V and 1k series instead - 4r100-deltas.md. Brake 92 is hot-at-all-times: 12 V when pressed." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 20.00 32.00 0) (effects (font (size 1.7 1.7)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "43c94770-ede6-4da4-acab-7aad6727236c"))
	(text "TR1 (ground-switched)" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 30.00 47.00 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "ed12d38b-e051-49a0-b485-4833b3f4c24d"))
